l_id": "toolu_01D4kXRN1tJ3n9d3ry9LoPtk", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53293, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01D4kXRN1tJ3n9d3ry9LoPtk", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54726, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0139ydMpuaeCHF7uu6bMAYoR", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55026, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0139ydMpuaeCHF7uu6bMAYoR", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55026, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0139ydMpuaeCHF7uu6bMAYoR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59426, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001, which pages on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was unhealthy in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed, so I picked v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. I retried once, which is safe because it targets the same known-good version, and it completed everywhere.\n- checkout-api now runs v2.3.0 in all regions, reports healthy and has an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- My first attempt to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had gone through, so there's no duplicate.\n- The summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state and two follow-ups: finding what broke v2.3.1 and what caused the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FBJmfA8ko3FGqJnhaU8mhb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PvJYykBNTiwxLbFJg1kdAc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Uo1NhEWxvuNEsuFSJcvV95", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01E9uPn7VkQKw7Qd1SbggrYN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. A rollback to the same healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01V7XGwCrkhPPq5g2Khtuzpo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GkFU5jeyQiQRxzswYHkyoC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y31r6o2vPY2togs7ztYzLD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01D4kXRN1tJ3n9d3ry9LoPtk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error halted it after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and of the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0139ydMpuaeCHF7uu6bMAYoR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001, which pages on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was unhealthy in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed, so I picked v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. I retried once, which is safe because it targets the same known-good version, and it completed everywhere.\n- checkout-api now runs v2.3.0 in all regions, reports healthy and has an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- My first attempt to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had gone through, so there's no duplicate.\n- The summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state and two follow-ups: finding what broke v2.3.1 and what caused the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}